# Binary files must never be line ending converted. core.autocrlf is true on at least one
# machine working on this repository, and a single CRLF inserted into a png corrupts it.
# An og-image.png was already lost this way once.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# These files are pinned by md5 by the drop tooling, so their bytes must be identical in the
# repository and in every working copy. With core.autocrlf true git would rewrite LF to CRLF on
# checkout, changing the digest of a file nobody edited and making every state check report an
# unknown file. The -text attribute switches that conversion off in both directions.
*.html -text
*.txt -text
*.xml -text
*.json -text
*.csv -text
*.js -text
*.sh -text
